Frozen arithmetic
- protocol probe: two logical Qwen calls on one fixed synthetic tool contract
- canary: 6 fault-family representatives x 2 models = 12 episodes
- formal: 24 tasks x 2 models x 3 runtimes x 2 conditions x 3 trials = 864 episodes

Hard gates
- protocol probe artifact must pass and contain digest-only provider evidence
- probe source hashes must match current probe/backend/contract code
- formal requires a valid 12-episode canary from the exact current source manifest
- missing, stale, invalid, or malformed prerequisite evidence is rejected before workspace creation
- analysis requires infrastructure validity and per-model quality readiness

Transport and budget policy
- maximum 8 logical model calls per episode
- maximum 20,000 input tokens and 8,192 output tokens per episode
- maximum 1,024 output tokens per logical response
- maximum USD 0.01 usage-value estimate per episode
- maximum 2 retries after the initial attempt, with 0.25/0.5 second delays
- retryable only: HTTP 429/500/502/503/504, transport error, invalid/timed-out response
- logical calls, physical attempts, and recovered retries are recorded separately
- unrecovered provider, usage-parse, or model-protocol failure invalidates the study

